# Auto-mount disabled on this board.
#
# This overwrites the stock rule of the same name. The stock version mounts
# every ext4 SD partition (oem, rootfs, data) on /mnt/sdcard, rw, as each is
# detected. That races our own mounters -- it grabs the oem partition so S20oem
# fails "Device or resource busy", leaving librockit.so unavailable and vicap
# unable to start -- and concurrently rw-mounting rootfs/data is a corruption
# risk. This board owns its partitions explicitly (S20linkmount, S20oem,
# S21uvrdata), so nothing here auto-mounts anything.
#
# NB: this eudev reads rules from /lib/udev/rules.d (and /run), NOT
# /etc/udev/rules.d -- its sysconfdir is a build-time path that doesn't exist on
# the device -- so the override must live here to take effect.
